{
  "id": "script-addons-s-loading-path",
  "title": "Script addons (-s) loading path",
  "kind": "callpath",
  "answers": [
    "How does -s script get loaded?",
    "Where is the scripts option registered?",
    "How does script hot reload work?"
  ],
  "body": "`-s` = `opts.make_parser(parser, \"scripts\", short=\"s\")` in `tools/cmdline.py:common_options`; option itself registered in `addons/script.py:ScriptLoader.load` (Sequence[str]); ScriptLoader is in `default_addons()`.\nFlow: `process_options` → `opts.update(scripts=[...])` → `changed` → `AddonManager._configure_all` → `ScriptLoader.configure(updated)` (only if \"scripts\" updated; rejects dupes, unloads removed, keeps order, creates `Script(path, reload=True)`, `master.addons.register(script)`, RunningHook if already running).\n`Script.__init__` expands path, raises OptionsError(\"No such script\") if missing; reload=True starts async `Script.watcher()` which defers first load, then polls mtime. `Script.loadscript` → `load_script(path)` imports as `__mitmproxy_script__.<name>` via SourceFileLoader with script dir temporarily on sys.path; errors go to `script_error_handler`; then `ctx.master.addons.register(ns)`.",
  "tags": [
    "scripts",
    "addons",
    "hot-reload"
  ],
